# Copy to mvp/.env.local. Keep real values out of Git and chat.
# Both values come from the Plaid Dashboard (Developers > Keys). The secret must
# match PLAID_ENV: the Sandbox secret for sandbox, the Production secret for production.
PLAID_CLIENT_ID=
PLAID_SECRET=
# sandbox = fictional test banks; production = your real bank accounts.
PLAID_ENV=sandbox
# The server always binds to this computer only.
PORT=4188
# Strongly recommended: an explicit folder for SQLite and its encryption key,
# outside the repository and outside OneDrive. Use a different folder for each
# environment; the app refuses to open a folder that holds the other kind of data.
# Default on Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\SaveUp\sandbox-mvp or %LOCALAPPDATA%\SaveUp\production
# SAVEUP_DATA_DIR=C:\dev\saveup-local-data\production
